    "role": "user",
    "content": "<problem>\nA chemical company is transporting their hydrogen using two different methods, high pressure tube trailers and liquefied hydrogen tankers. The first method is a high-pressure tube trailer which can transport 50 cubic meters each per trip at a cost of $500. The second method is using liquefied hydrogen tankers which can transport 30 cubic meters each per trip at a cost of $200. The company needs to transport at least 1000 cubic meters of hydrogen and they have budget of $3750 available. In addition, the number of transports done by the high pressure tube trailer method has to be less than the number of transports done by the liquefied hydrogen tanker method. How many of each transportation method should they use to minimize the total number of trips?\n</problem>\n\n<previous_model>\n{\"variables\":[{\"name\":\"high_pressure_tube_trailer_trips\",\"lower\":0,\"upper\":null,\"integer\":true},{\"name\":\"liquefied_hydrogen_tanker_trips\",\"lower\":0,\"upper\":null,\"integer\":true}],\"objective\":{\"sense\":\"min\",\"terms\":[{\"var\":\"high_pressure_tube_trailer_trips\",\"coef\":1},{\"var\":\"liquefied_hydrogen_tanker_trips\",\"coef\":1}]},\"constraints\":[{\"name\":\"transport_requirement\",\"terms\":[{\"var\":\"high_pressure_tube_trailer_trips\",\"coef\":50},{\"var\":\"liquefied_hydrogen_tanker_trips\",\"coef\":30}],\"sense\":\">=\",\"rhs\":1000},{\"name\":\"budget\",\"terms\":[{\"var\":\"high_pressure_tube_trailer_trips\",\"coef\":500},{\"var\":\"liquefied_hydrogen_tanker_trips\",\"coef\":200}],\"sense\":\"<=\",\"rhs\":3750},{\"name\":\"trip_count_order\",\"terms\":[{\"var\":\"high_pressure_tube_trailer_trips\",\"coef\":1},{\"var\":\"liquefied_hydrogen_tanker_trips\",\"coef\":-1}],\"sense\":\"<=\",\"rhs\":-1}]}\n</previous_model>\n\n<feedback>\nThe solver found the model infeasible: no values satisfy every constraint. These constraints can't all hold at once: 'transport_requirement', 'budget'. Check them against the problem text for a reversed direction (<= vs >=), a wrong number, or a requirement the text doesn't state. Don't drop or loosen a requirement the text does state just to get a solution: some problems are infeasible as written.\n</feedback>\n\nReturn a corrected model. If you're sure the previous model already says what the problem says, return it unchanged."
